y fundamental change called  upon by the street to be a conspiracy  and hence I'm afraid as they did today  earlier when a bunch of thugs went into  the street and started to break you know  various protests that this might  continue in different ways despite the  fact that the head of Hezbollah in his  last speech asked his followers from  Hezbollah to clear out of the public  squares and yet apparently apparently  secretly or or or implicitly they're  sending out those thugs in order or  there's activists let me call them so I  don't sound tutorial izing in any which  way the activists of the various groups  that Hezbollah are going down the  streets and one of the worst case  scenarios in Lebanon if as Hezbollah  leader said will be one Street against  another Street we've seen that after the  assassination of Rafik Hariri between  the so-called March 7 and March 14  movement that paralyzed the country we  don't want to see the Lebanese don't  want to see in Lebanon paralyzed it want  to see it moving forward so certainly it  wants to avoid at every possible cost a  street against the street a street  against an organized political party  that does not want change in Lebanon all  right Marwan Bashara thank you

